0015: rewind mode for test harnesses, off unless bridge.conf sets rewindMode = True in both copies. A test host snapshots the game process and later puts its memory back; the server then returns to the D3D9 state of the snapshot, exactly or not at all. At the end of a Present the client parks with the send locks of both channels held, so no other thread of the game can send, and passes each request of the host on as one synchronous Bridge_Rewind command. At a snapshot the server copies its handle tables, the device state and every render target and depth surface. While the snapshot is held it defers destroys of the objects alive at it and keeps the old contents of a buffer or surface before the first write, up to rewindMaxKeptMB. On a rewind it brings back destroyed objects, lets go of new ones, puts contents, device state and data queue positions back, and reads no command until the client's process is back at the snapshot. What it cannot put back exactly makes it give the snapshot up and refuse (server/rewind_mode.h). With the option off the client makes no cooperation block, the server takes no snapshot, and each hook is one test of a flag that is never set. Tests: test/rtx/unit/test_rewind_server.cpp and test_rewind_device.cpp (native/remix-bridge/test-rewind.cmd).
Applies after 0001-0014 on NVIDIAGameWorks/dxvk-remix f35b86a (bridge/ only).
